## Causal Graph

```
CAUSES: [CASE-FLOW-DECISION] -> [CASE-FLOW-FAIL]
ENABLES: [CASE-P5-MAPPING] -> [CASE-CONTEXT-FOR-CHANGE]
```

## [CASE-WRAPPED-VALUE] A property value WRAPPED across physical lines

- requirement: a wrapped value is ONE value -- the parser joins each continuation
  line to the head, collapsing the newline to a single space and keeping the
  author's internal spacing verbatim
- status: active

## [CASE-WRAPPED-EXCLUSION] An indented BULLET under a valued head is not a continuation

- boundary: the indented bullet below opens its own structure and must not be folded
  into this value
  - a sub-bullet is new structure, not a wrapped sentence

## [CASE-ID-TABLE] A table whose first column is an identifier column is DATA

| ID | Requirement | verify.machine |
|----|-------------|----------------|
| CTRL-T1 | a wrapped value is joined, not truncated | test_wrapped_value_is_joined |
| CTRL-T2 | an ID table reaches the graph | test_id_table_rows_become_properties |

## [CASE-PLAIN-TABLE] A table with NO identifier column stays ignorable

| Layer | What it does |
|-------|--------------|
| narrative | decoration, not data |
| grid | still decoration |

## Compliance (an UNTAGGED heading -- the table below has no node of its own)

| ID | Requirement | verify.machine |
|----|-------------|----------------|
| CTRL-T3 | an ID table under an untagged heading lands on its ANCESTOR node | test_orphan_id_table_attaches_to_ancestor |

## [CASE-QUAL-PAREN] SL-21 a PARENTHETICAL qualifier in the KEY REGION

- requirement (qualified): a parenthetical qualifier before the colon is FLAGGED, never guessed
- delta: (leading paren in value) form (measured): the paren is in the VALUE, so it parses
- status: negative-case

## [CASE-QUAL-DASH] SL-22 an EM-DASH qualifier in the KEY REGION

- requirement — dashed: an em-dash qualifier before the colon is FLAGGED, never guessed
- boundary: an em-dash inside a value — and a colon after it: both stay in the value
- status: negative-case

## 23. SL-23 a citation [CASE-CITED-NOT-DECLARED] hijacks the id declared at the end [CASE-ID-HIJACK]

- status: negative-case

